; A rule cycle whose ENTRY POINT is the collection rule leaves the referring rule holding a NOMINAL
; `Rust(ident)` reference to a `RustStructType::Table`/`Array` — a struct that emits no impls of its
; own, only a rust typedef onto the collection. Every generation site that dispatches on a struct
; reference must therefore treat it as the collection; the ones that did not aborted generation
; (`cbor_types`) or emitted `.serialize()`/`::deserialize()` on a `BTreeMap`/`Vec`.
;
; Rule order is what decides which reference path a spec takes, so each block below fixes it by
; naming its root: `<x>_holder` names the COLLECTION for the nominal blocks and names the UNION for
; the control. Both spellings must generate the same working code.

; --- nominal reference (cycle entered at the collection rule) ---
; Plain table. `nom_val` is parsed before `nom_map` registers its alias, so the arm is `Rust(NomMap)`.
nom_holder = [nom_map]
nom_val = nom_map / int
nom_map = { * text => nom_val }

; Array flavor — the same class through `RustStructType::Array` (`pub type ArrList = Vec<ArrVal>`).
arr_holder = [arr_list]
arr_val = arr_list / int
arr_list = [* arr_val]

; `@duplicates preserve` — the per-rule policy lives on the STRUCT, and a nominal reference carries
; none of it, so the emission has to read it back off the struct or the pair-map twin
; (`PairMap<String, PresVal>`) is emitted with loose-table code. This is the shape the corpus
; `table_preserve.mdmap` row exercises (pre-Conway `transaction_metadata`).
pres_holder = [pres_map]
pres_val = pres_map / int
pres_map = { * text => pres_val } ; @duplicates preserve

; `{+ }` — same argument for the occurrence bounds, which select the `NonEmptyMap` twin.
nem_holder = [nem_map]
nem_val = nem_map / int
nem_map = { + text => nem_val }

; Union-KEYED table — the map's DOMAIN, not just its range, is the recursive union (the Cardano
; `transaction_metadata` shape). The keys-list wasm wrapper is minted from the domain, so this is the
; spelling that has to answer for a domain naming a struct that is itself the collection.
;
key_holder = [key_map]
key_val = key_map / int / bytes / text
key_map = { * key_val => key_val }

; Union-KEYED table in the UNION-rooted ordering — the same three rules with the cycle rooted at the
; union, which orders the table's registration BEFORE its named domain exists as a struct. The
; keys-list wrapper cannot be named from an ident that is registered as nothing yet, so its mint is
; deferred to `finalize_deferred_table_keys_lists`; the wasm half of that (mint/reference agreement)
; is pinned by `union_rooted_recursive_union_keyed_table_mints_its_keys_list`, and this block holds
; the ordering to the same compile-and-wire floor as its collection-rooted twin above.
ukey_holder = [ukey_val]
ukey_val = ukey_map / int / bytes / text
ukey_map = { * ukey_val => ukey_val }

; The consumer's CIP-25 metadatum shape in that union-rooted ordering: the union carries an ARRAY arm
; and the table takes `@duplicates preserve`, so recursion composes with a rule-position directive —
; the deferred mint must leave the policy (the `PairMap` twin) alone.
upres_holder = [upres_val]
upres_val = upres_map / [* upres_val] / int / bytes / text
upres_map = { * upres_val => upres_val } ; @duplicates preserve

; --- resolved-alias reference (cycle entered at the union rule) — the CONTROL ---
; Identical rules to the `nom_` block but rooted at the union, which orders `res_map` first. This
; spelling generated and compiled before any of the above was fixed; it is the byte-level target for
; what the nominal path should emit, and it is here so a future change that re-resolves or
; un-nominalizes references cannot silently break it.
res_holder = [res_val]
res_val = res_map / int
res_map = { * text => res_val }
